artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $D$ be a bounded planar domain whose boundary is a simple closed path in the triangular lattice (with mesh going to zero). Mark two points on $\partial D$, each being the midpoint of a lattice edge, that split $\partial D$ into two complementary arcs $\partial_+$ and $\partial_-$. Consider the uniform probability measure on functions $h$ defined on the vertices of $D$ taking values in the odd integers, subject to the following constraints:
(i) $h \equiv 1$ on vertices of $\partial_+$;
(ii) $h \equiv -1$ on vertices of $\partial_-$;
(iii) $|h(v) - h(u)| \in \{0, 2\}$ for every pair of neighboring vertices $u, v$.

Extend $h$ to all of $D$ by affine interpolation on each triangular face. Let $\gamma$ be the unique connected component of $h^{-1}(0)$ that contains the two midpoints of $\partial_+ \cap \partial_-$; this $\gamma$ is a simple path joining these two boundary points.

Prove or disprove: as the lattice mesh tends to zero (with the domain and marked boundary points approximating a fixed conformal configuration), the random interface $\gamma$ converges in law to chordal $\mathrm{SLE}_4$ in $D$ from one marked point to the other, and the random function $h$, viewed as a distribution on $D$, converges in law to the Gaussian free field on $D$ with boundary values $+1$ on $\partial_+$ and $-1$ on $\partial_-$.

